<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>GTA VI launch-day productivity audit</title>
<style>
$css
</style>
</head>
<body>
<section class="page page-report">
  <div class="kicker">Independent audit · GTA VI launch day</div>
  <div class="title">The launch-day productivity claim, checked against its own math</div>
  <div class="block">$claim_block</div>
  <div class="block">$range_block</div>
  <div class="block">$superbowl_block</div>
  <div class="block"><div class="k">Hard anchors</div>$anchors_block</div>
  <div class="block cant">
    <div class="k">What we can’t measure</div>
    <p>Actual sick calls (official absence data lags by about a month), actual delivery orders (private data), and actual lost output (this is a model, by construction). Most one-day absence output is deferred, not destroyed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><div class="sources">Sources: $sources_small</div><div class="lock">$lock_line</div></div>
</section>

<section class="page page-table">
  <div class="kicker">Model table</div>
  <div class="title">Every input, its value, kind and source</div>
  <div class="block">$inputs_table</div>
  <div class="k">Case grid: absences × output per worker-day</div>
  <div class="block">$grid</div>
  $context_block
  <div class="foot"><div class="lock">$lock_line</div></div>
</section>

<section class="page page-method">
  <div class="kicker">Methodology</div>
  <div class="title">Formulas as written, locked before launch</div>
  <div class="block">$formulas</div>
  $precedent_block
  <div class="block">
    <div class="k">Method lock</div>
    <p>The model configuration and formula code were hashed and locked before launch-day data existed. Any later change to either breaks the hash and stops the build.</p>
    <p class="hash">$lock_hash_full</p>
  </div>
  <div class="block">
    <div class="k">Limits</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Absences are triangulated from platform data and surveys, never directly counted.</li>
      <li>Survey intent overstates behavior; the high case is labeled as such.</li>
      <li>Output per worker-day is an average; the dollar figures are a model, not a measurement.</li>
      <li>Figures labeled proxy are directional evidence only.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><div class="lock">$lock_line</div></div>
</section>
</body>
</html>
